  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved labour administration, wages systems and workplace compliance policies in Vanuatu</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved labour administration and wage systems, aligns with  the realization of strengthening workplace compliance and wage systems in Vanuatu and with international labour standards, which directly supports Protection at work for all. By enhancing these systems, Vanuatu ensures that all workers, including women, young people, and persons with disabilities, have access to full and productive employment. This alignment is essential for achieving the goal of equal pay for work of equal value by 2030. Improved compliance safeguards workers&apos; rights and promotes a fairer labour market, contributing to the overall economic growth and social justice in the region. By adopting evidence-based wage policies, including adequate statutory or negotiated minimum wages, Vanuatu contributex to ensuring fair compensation for workers and advancing universal social protection and a more equitable and secure labour market for all citizens. ILO has partnered with the Vanuatu tripartite partners in these initiatives targeting all workers as beneficiaries. In addition to this, ILO is assisting with developing Vanuatu&apos;s Decent Work Country Programme (DWCP) which will cover 2026-2029. Beneficiaries for this will be the tripartite partners and the public in general.</narrative>
  </description>
